entor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WAKITA AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA KAZUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKEI, KATSUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KURA, HISAAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAKINO, HIROAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MURAMATSU, KAZUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WAKITA, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, KAZUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A shaft member (1) and an outer periphery member (2) disposed on the outer periphery of the shaft member (1) are joined together by a spline (3) where a tooth (31) on the shaft member (1) and a tooth (32) on the outer periphery member (2) are fitted together. On one axial end side of the spline (3), the trough (31a) of the tooth (31) of the shaft member (1) is diametrically increased to form a diameter-increased region (S1), and provided in this diameter-increased region (S1) is a fitting portion (F) for the tooth (31) of the shaft member (1) and the tooth (32) of the outer periphery member (2).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Un arbre (1) et un élément (2) placé à la périphérie extérieure de l'arbre (1) sont reliés par une cannelure (3), une dent (31) de l'arbre (1) et une dent de l'élément périphérique (2) étant en contact. A l'une des extrémités axiales de la cannelure le creux (31a) de la dent (31) de l'arbre (1) croît diamétralement de manière à former une zone (S1) de diamètre élargi qui présente une partie (F) recevant la dent (31) de l'arbre (1) et la dent de l'élément périphérique (2).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>